//? Title: TD(0): actual sampled bootstrap updates and honest episode outcomes
//? Subtitle: Actual canonical histories, retained original fixtures and explicit controls
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Temporal-difference prediction evaluates a fixed policy using actual one-step
environment transitions. The original five-interior-state random walk retains
its callback RNG, zero initialization and episode snapshots; real update and
episode histories replace repeated report-side learning loops.
)

\toc

> Mechanism and mathematical scope

At observed(s,r,next,terminal), let successor=0 if terminal, otherwise the
current V(next). Compute target=r+gamma*successor, error=target-V(s), then
V(s)<-V(s)+alpha*error. Read the successor before updating, including self
transitions. This evaluates the supplied policy and does not improve it. In the
fair five-state walk with right-exit reward1 and gamma1, the mathematical
reference is V(k)=k/6 for k1..5 and zero terminal continuation. The original
code initializes values to0, not0.5. Constant alpha=.1 gives a noisy tracking
estimate; finite-sample errors need not decrease monotonically and exact
asymptotic convergence is not promised. Classical prediction theorems require
suitable task, visitation and step-size assumptions.

> A tiny actual producing history

The table and native concept diagram read the same producing execution. Every
block below is a complete editable C++ program.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/td_learning_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    namespace a = dm::algorithms;
    namespace g = dm::graphics;
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    a::TabularEnvironment env{1, 1, [] {
        return std::size_t{0};
    }, [](std::size_t, std::size_t) {
        return a::StepResult{0, 2, true};
    }
    };
    a::RLParameters p;
    p.episodes = 3;
    p.learning_rate = .5;
    auto r = a::td_prediction_trace(env, {0}, p);
    std::print("| actual episode | value before | terminal successor | target | error | value after |\n| " "---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (const auto &s : r.steps)
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", s.episode, s.before,
                   s.successor, s.target, s.error, s.after);
    g::Diagram concept_diagram(48, 1100);
    concept_diagram.node("n0", {0, 0}, "Actual terminal reward2; initial value0");
    concept_diagram.node("n1", {5, 0},
                         std::format("{} actual TD updates", r.transitions));
    concept_diagram.node("n2", {10, 0},
                         std::format("Actual final value {}", r.result.value[0]));
    concept_diagram.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
    concept_diagram.save_svg("build/td_learning_tiny.svg");
}
```
